{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531486-the-hypnos-institute","id":1531486,"title":"The Hypnos Institute","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-25T17:26:04-08:00","id":1531486,"title":"The Hypnos Institute","content":"I have recently come up with this antagonist idea for Changeling themed around a series of sleep clinics that also act as fronts for researching the Dreaming. It is called the Hypnos Institute.<br /> <br /> The person who started all of this was one Dr. Ivan Hristov, a Yugoslavian Sleep Doctor during the Cold War, was decorated for his research into insomnia and dreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> He was called by the Yugoslavian or Soviet government to treat the daughter of a top official talking of dreams of giants, and elves, and goblins, and dragons that were keeping her up at night. To make matters worse, her dreams seemingly began to leak into her waking hours to, concerning her Father, a top General. Fearing that her daughter could be taken away and placed in a facility, the General commissioned Dr. Hristov with finding out what was causing his daughters' dreams and eliminating them<br /> <br /> <br /> The patient, Anya, was actually a Childling who had recently became a Changeling and was still getting used to her new life when she first met Dr. Hristov. Hristov subjected her to rigorous sleep studies, questioning, and other experimental techniques to try and find the source of her Dreams, but found himself becoming more and more consumed with interest in his young patients imaginary world and how detailed it was.<br /> <br /> <br /> Eventually the good Doctor went from trying to eliminate the Girl's dreams to studying her dreams, unintentionally learning more and more about the Dreaming as he continued. By the time the experiments finally killed young Anya's fae self Dr. Hristov had enough information about The Dreaming to fill a notebook, but never got to publish the results before being killed by a vengeful Troll.<br /> <br /> <br /> His Journal somehow survived the Yugoslavian Civil War and ended up in the hands of his Grandson, Juri. Juri, a sleep doctor who recently immigrated to America, decided to continue his Grandfather's research and is currently the head of the Hypnos Institute, a series of clinics that advertise themselves as specializing in treating overactive dreamers, but are actually seeking to learn more about the Dreaming and it's residents .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would like thoughts on this idea and suggestions and how to make it fit in better with Changeling and possibly ideas for a end goal for their research","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T17:59:45-08:00","id":1531487,"title":"","content":"Look, it's a kind of generic idea, but what about forming a military initiative? Like Juri is being funded by a secret anti-changeling or anti-dreaming initiative, the group would have been formed after 9/11 in response to various unusual incidents caused by the Thalain (many appeared after that day, and they didn't know what it was Thalaim or Kithain at the time), not knowing how to contain these incidents and distrusting external forces, they searched for any clue and this led them to Juri's research which seemed to be the most promising result, having said that the ultimate goal of their research would be a way of controlling dreaming, as they see it as something quite dangerous, ultimately they would destroy it if they could.<br /> <br /> As for possible research results, I imagine the basics would be fine, like discovering the effect of cold iron, accidental or purposeful creation of Dauthain, or extracting glamor from a changeling and using it in some way. In fact, just to be clear, some of them would treat dreaming as an illness or contamination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T21:14:21-08:00","id":1531492,"title":"","content":"Seems like a fairly typical Autumn Person antagonist akin to Dr Anton Stark. &quot;Typical&quot; does not mean bad, but it seems to slot very close to Anton Stark. Not identical because your description implies that Ivan &amp; Juri Hristov seem to think their notes on the Dreaming indicate that there is something &quot;real&quot; (even if not physical) about the delusions of their patients. I would built on that distinction. <br /> <br /> Determine what exactly Juri Hristov thinks about the &quot;Dreaming&quot;. Is it mass psychosis? Some archtypical reality revealed in multiple dreams? Some alternate dimension these people contact? Something else?<br /> <br /> Once you know how Hristov views the &quot;Dreaming&quot;, I think you'll have more ideas on what he might do about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T23:16:16-08:00","id":1531493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531486-the-hypnos-institute#post1531486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have recently come up with this antagonist idea for Changeling themed around a series of sleep clinics that also act as fronts for researching the Dreaming. It is called the Hypnos Institute.<br /> <br /> The person who started all of this was one Dr. Ivan Hristov, a Yugoslavian Sleep Doctor during the Cold War, was decorated for his research into insomnia and dreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> He was called by the Yugoslavian or Soviet government to treat the daughter of a top official talking of dreams of giants, and elves, and goblins, and dragons that were keeping her up at night. To make matters worse, her dreams seemingly began to leak into her waking hours to, concerning her Father, a top General. Fearing that her daughter could be taken away and placed in a facility, the General commissioned Dr. Hristov with finding out what was causing his daughters' dreams and eliminating them</div> </div> </div> </div>Little historical quibble - while post-WWII Yugoslavia was indeed a socialist republic, it was <b>not </b>a soviet subject in no way or manner, having liberated their country from nazi occupation mostly on their own, being one of the founders, alongside India &amp; Egypt, of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-Aligned_Movement\" target=\"_blank\">Non-Aligned Movement</a> in the early Cold War Era, among other things.<br /> <br /> So, you might want to look into some <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warsaw_Pact#Members\" target=\"_blank\">Warsaw Pact</a> member states instead. I think Romania, that had no war but went through a quick and bloody popular <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanian_revolution\" target=\"_blank\">revolution </a>involving the execution of local dictator (and inspired everybody else to speed up their reform processes), might make for a good alternative, though some of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post-Soviet_states\" target=\"_blank\">ex-soviet republics</a> might work too i guess.<br /> <br /> Supposing that is even important, that is - lots of countries with places where influential/rich people will throw a problematic relative into &quot;an extended stress treatment&quot; or somesuch, close doors, lose the key and forget, with public none the wiser. Money and discretion grease all too many dirty gears....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-26-2024, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T15:45:26-08:00","id":1531553,"title":"","content":"Oh I knew Yugoslavia wasn't part of the Soviet Union, guess I made a formatting or typing mistake. Romania actually does make perfect sense for Ivan's home country though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T16:22:50-07:00","id":1535872,"title":"","content":"The whole problem here is, the trope of the mental health institution that kills imagination aged very poorly.<br /> <br /> My first question being: if Ivan Hristov actually saw something in her dreams, why and how did his research killed her fae self?<br /> <br /> He seems pretty low on Banality to me, and the whole research looks quite healthy on Glamour.<br /> <br /> And what about Juri Hristov? A modern day psychiatrist is even less prone to be simply killing imagination, at least not someone involved in state-of-the-art research.<br /> <br /> I think your idea works better today as something related to Nightmare, maybe with the research fuelling the Thallain or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T05:12:54-07:00","id":1535893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531486-the-hypnos-institute?p=1535872#post1535872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole problem here is, the trope of the mental health institution that kills imagination aged very poorly.<br /> <br /> My first question being: if Ivan Hristov actually saw something in her dreams, why and how did his research killed her fae self?<br /> <br /> He seems pretty low on Banality to me, and the whole research looks quite healthy on Glamour.<br /> <br /> And what about Juri Hristov? A modern day psychiatrist is even less prone to be simply killing imagination, at least not someone involved in state-of-the-art research.<br /> <br /> I think your idea works better today as something related to Nightmare, maybe with the research fuelling the Thallain or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand correctly how Changelings work, the research would have killed the fairy part because it doesn't see it as something magical, but as a scientific phenomenon which makes it somewhat banal, and I'm guessing the fairy part didn't die for lack of glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T14:21:07-07:00","id":1535921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531486-the-hypnos-institute?p=1535893#post1535893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I understand correctly how Changelings work, the research would have killed the fairy part because it doesn't see it as something magical, but as a scientific phenomenon which makes it somewhat banal, and I'm guessing the fairy part didn't die for lack of glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's neither how Changeling or science work. Changeling isn't Mage.<br /> <br /> Glamour is about imagination and sense of wonder. It's opposite is apathy and sameness. Children aren't usually low Banality because they believe in magic (many, by the way, do not), but because they easily see wonder and possibility in the simplest things.<br /> <br /> Banality usually accrues in places and situations where creativity is stifled, specially if it is on purpose. Where new ideas are seen as a waste of time, and people are expected to follow strict procedures.<br /> <br /> Any profession or endeavor can be of high or low Banality, and even actively produce Glamour, depending on the attitudes of the people involved.<br /> <br /> Here we have scientists going out of their way to examine the dreams of a child and the possibilities they open, even going against the wishes of a parent that only wants her &quot;normalization&quot;. This seems like something that would generate Glamour, not Banality. In fact, this Changeling is safer (as far as Banality goes) with the research team than with the worried parent.<br /> <br /> Note: the parent isn't necessarily a problem, either. Although it is likely and a trope in CtD, we're given a father that became worried mostly when the girl became dysfunctional. While most Changelings aren't exactly highly functional people, by itself this isn't Banality, but possibly an actual problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T14:51:03-07:00","id":1535924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531486-the-hypnos-institute?p=1535921#post1535921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's neither how Changeling or science work. Changeling isn't Mage.<br /> <br /> Glamour is about imagination and sense of wonder. It's opposite is apathy and sameness. Children aren't usually low Banality because they believe in magic (many, by the way, do not), but because they easily see wonder and possibility in the simplest things.<br /> <br /> Banality usually accrues in places and situations where creativity is stifled, specially if it is on purpose. Where new ideas are seen as a waste of time, and people are expected to follow strict procedures.<br /> <br /> Any profession or endeavor can be of high or low Banality, and even actively produce Glamour, depending on the attitudes of the people involved.<br /> <br /> Here we have scientists going out of their way to examine the dreams of a child and the possibilities they open, even going against the wishes of a parent that only wants her &quot;normalization&quot;. This seems like something that would generate Glamour, not Banality. In fact, this Changeling is safer (as far as Banality goes) with the research team than with the worried parent.<br /> <br /> Note: the parent isn't necessarily a problem, either. Although it is likely and a trope in CtD, we're given a father that became worried mostly when the girl became dysfunctional. While most Changelings aren't exactly highly functional people, by itself this isn't Banality, but possibly an actual problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your explanation makes sense, but I still believe that you trying to use a scientific process to deal with glamor is a banal process, as you said Glamor comes from the sense of wonder and if we apply the idea to this context, it would be if a child believed that it was special or that the fire that lights up in the stove appeared by magic, but a doctor appears who gives an explanation for the phenomenon and the child realizes that it was not special, it was simply mundane, the child may even insist on the fantasy, but the The adult will continue to contradict her until the point that she feels bad for thinking like that and finally comes the banality, understand? In the case of changelings they may even believe they were delusional.<br /> <br /> One thing that came to mind now, there is also a chance that with some experiment, he removed the glamor by force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T15:39:54-07:00","id":1535925,"title":"","content":"By your account, a child with an interest in science would be Banal, regardless if they marvel at new discoveries or if science class flare their imagination with thoughts of traveling the outer space or the deep ocean, if they fantasize about tiny or gigantic animals.<br /> <br /> That's not how children work, and not how Changeling works. Again, it's not Mage. It's not about belief. It isn't Werewolf either, it's not about Wild and Weaver. It does have some correlation with those, but not causation.<br /> <br /> Glamour is about creativity. The process is secondary, what matters is if it is done with passion and curiosity. And this passion may be towards anything.<br /> <br /> Changelings derive energy from inspiration and passion, not from whatever results they achieve. They're magical because they are, not because someone believed, but their magic is fueled by those emotions.<br /> <br /> And I will repeat, the trope of the Banal Mental Health Institution is one that aged badly, C20 even directly acknowledges that. Also it ignores how much creative thinking and care is involved in scientific research, or how much modern mental health care works to help people embrace creativity and their emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}